 "identification_note": "Observational: return is predicted from the individual's own past activity (persistence and heterogeneity). Nothing here identifies what would make an individual return more often.",
 "extrapolation_limits": "Evidence: KuaiRand-Pure (27,285 anonymised Kuaishou users chosen by the KuaiRand authors (China, 2022); interactions only with the 7,583 videos of the random-exposure pool); activity = at least one logged exposure that day in the standard or random-exposure log (Kuaishou app, 2022-04-22..05-08). The simulator may use the model for the daily probability that an individual comes back to a feed platform given its recent activity pattern, and the fitted relation between recent activity and return (habit persistence). It may NOT infer: absolute activity levels of other platforms (an active day here requires a logged pool-video exposure, and the random-insertion rate rose during the period, so detected activity rises over time); long-horizon churn beyond 17 days; effects of notifications, content quality or social ties (not inputs); populations other than this selected sample of Kuaishou users. The training days include the 2022-04-30..05-04 Labour Day holiday in China, the test days do not.",
 "feature_map": {
  "active_days_7d": "number of the previous 7 days on which the individual was active on the platform",
  "days_since_last_active": "days since the individual's last active day, capped at 14",
  "log_rows_7d": "log1p(feed exposures in the previous 7 days); map by quantile (dataset logs only a sample of exposures)",
  "log_sessions_7d": "log1p(sessions in the previous 7 days; a session ends after 30 idle minutes); map by quantile",
  "active_yesterday": "1 if the individual was active the previous day",
  "weekend": "1 on Saturdays and Sundays"
 },
